    "name": "Sea and Soil",
    "steam_appid": 3875480,
    "required_age": 0,
    "is_free": false,
    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><picture><source srcset=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3875480/extras/1ccbcf90326daccd6dced2ce57ffc9b7.poster.avif?t=1753068349\" media=\"(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)\"><img src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3875480/extras/1ccbcf90326daccd6dced2ce57ffc9b7.gif?t=1753068349\" class=\"bb_img\" /></picture></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Overview</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You're headed to the Sea Breeze Healing Center, the location of the teen winter camp your father signed you up for. Once there, you must explore the hospital, talk to patients, and hold out until your father picks you up...</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Features</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A game with some horror elements set in a hospital</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Multiple endings depending on your early choices</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A compact but dense map designed by a directionally challenged developer</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Cute pixelated graphics</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Easy difficulty level</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >How to play</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Move: \u2191\u2192\u2190\u2193</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Jump: Shift</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Menu: Q</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Bag: I</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Zoom: L</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Save: Pink gramophone</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >From the creators</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The story is different depending on the early fork in the road, and there are parts that don't make sense if you only go one way, so we recommend playing through both.</p>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><picture><source srcset=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3875480/extras/1ccbcf90326daccd6dced2ce57ffc9b7.poster.avif?t=1753068349\" media=\"(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)\"><img src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3875480/extras/1ccbcf90326daccd6dced2ce57ffc9b7.gif?t=1753068349\" class=\"bb_img\" /></picture></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Overview</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You're headed to the Sea Breeze Healing Center, the location of the teen winter camp your father signed you up for. Once there, you must explore the hospital, talk to patients, and hold out until your father picks you up...</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Features</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A game with some horror elements set in a hospital</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Multiple endings depending on your early choices</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A compact but dense map designed by a directionally challenged developer</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Cute pixelated graphics</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Easy difficulty level</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >How to play</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Move: \u2191\u2192\u2190\u2193</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Jump: Shift</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Menu: Q</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Bag: I</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Zoom: L</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Save: Pink gramophone</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >From the creators</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The story is different depending on the early fork in the road, and there are parts that don't make sense if you only go one way, so we recommend playing through both.</p>",
    "short_description": "You're headed to the Sea Breeze Healing Center, the location of the teen winter camp your father signed you up for. Once there, you must explore the hospital, talk to patients, and hold out until your father picks you up...",
